<root BTCPP_format="4">
  <!-- Take one elevator to a place on the other floor, from floor 2 or floor 1, with door preemption both ways.
       PARAMETERS, set by the planner in its answer (use_tree with goal="{...}"; from a session, planner_cli answer
       with the use-tree and param options):
         elevator    the elevator to ride, the prefix of its places and areas in the places file, e.g. elevator1 or freight
         goal        the place to end at, as a place key, e.g. {elevator1_target_floor_2} or {freight_hall_floor_1}
         goal_floor  the floor of that place, "1" or "2". Leave it out: the planner sets it from the places file
                     floors table by the place's z (planner.fill_floor_parameters); a value that disagrees is refused
       The rest follows from elevator and goal_floor ("floor settings"): the robot must stand on the other floor
       (at_floor checks it), the places <elevator>_<position>_floor_<n> of the call panel and the inside panel of its
       floor, the floor button, and the door-out place of the goal floor. set_elevator then names the elevator to the
       stack, so inside_cabin and door_open use its areas <elevator>_cabin and <elevator>_hall.
       1. Walk to the call panel (through its preapproach place when the floor has one) and press the call button (the
          operator may press it too). door_open (lidar) is checked on every tick: once the door opens, the walk or the
          press is halted, the arms are released and, 1 s later, the robot walks straight to the inside panel.
       2. In the cabin: press the goal floor button (each look resets the EKF). Checked on every tick: inside_cabin, at_floor
          {goal_floor} and door_open. Once all three hold, the press or the wait is halted and the arms are released;
          once LIO leaves elevator mode, the robot walks out on its own pose: the door-out place of the goal floor, a
          relocalization there, then {goal}.
       Both presses use the press slot press_panel_button (stance_check, press_button, press_judge, recover_once).
       Each press slot starts from its panel's base offset (elevator.xml); an offset_retry sets the next one.
       Needs the Thor's grounding. Needs slam_elevatorlio and door_state_node that take places_file and /elevator_name. -->
  <BehaviorTree ID="freight_elevator_go_to_place">
    <Sequence>
      <Sequence name="parameters">          <!-- the planner fills these three -->
        <SetBlackboard output_key="elevator" value="elevator1"/>
        <SetBlackboard output_key="goal" value="{elevator1_target_floor_2}"/>
        <SetBlackboard output_key="goal_floor" value="2"/>
      </Sequence>
      <SubTree ID="ride_to_goal"/>      <!-- floor settings, the ride and the walk to goal: subtrees/elevator.xml -->
    </Sequence>
  </BehaviorTree>

  <include path="subtrees/elevator.xml"/>
  <include path="subtrees/press.xml"/>
  <include path="subtrees/walk.xml"/>
</root>
